.gitignore

# Generated by install-rbtv.py
AGENTS.md

# Added by bootstrap.py (admin mode)
/workflows/build-rbtv-component/data/CLAUDE.md

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# npm build artifact. The committed manifests (package.json + package-lock.json) are the
# reproducible source of truth; node_modules/ is materialized per machine by `npm ci` and is
# never committed (task 7.51). Matched at ANY depth — the ignite module root is the first
# folder to carry a manifest, but it will not be the last.
**/node_modules/

# Done-gate evidence (proof-of-work sheets + captures) — local only, never shipped.
# Matched at ANY depth: rbtv-done-gate writes to docs/done-gate-evidence/ at a repo
# root by default, but sub-app docs dirs (e.g. studio/hypresent/docs/) have also held it.
**/done-gate-evidence/

# Real-deck test fixtures (large local decks for hypresent e2e/unit suites) — local only,
# substitutable per machine, never shipped (a real client deck must not enter repo history).
tecer-gsmm-introduction*.html

# Probe captures (G-171). A probe writes its verdict into an adjacent `<name>.out`. These were
# tracked, and preserve mode (G-163) then restored each one's bytes AND its mtime after every
# run — which stopped the churn and froze every capture into a snapshot nothing would refresh.
# `probe-error-map-drift.out` read "1 drift finding" while the live probe reported 15, and a seat
# read the file, took it for its own run's output, and reported the debt 15x too small. The
# detector was never fooled; the PERSON was, and nothing on disk could tell them.
# Untracked, a capture is unambiguously the LAST RUN's output. Nothing is lost: git history keeps
# every capture ever committed, and probe-suite archives each run under the workspace `.rbtv/`
# runtime root. Probes still WRITE them, so the 7.50 staleness grading (which reads mtime from
# disk, never git) is unaffected. Scope is probe captures ONLY, in EVERY module — `ignite/deploy/*.out`
# are one-off harness outputs preserve mode never touched, and stay tracked; they sit directly in
# `deploy/`, so a `probes/`-anchored pattern never matches them.
# Widened from `ignite/**/probes/*.out` on 2026-08-11: the ignite-scoped form silently left
# `orchestration/`'s only capture tracked (a rule never untracks what is already tracked, so it also
# needed a `git rm --cached` to take effect), and a second per-module line would have reopened the
# same gap for whichever module grew probes next.
**/probes/*.out

# save-coord.py staging artifacts — transient by design ("a candidate nobody names
# destroys nothing", save-coord.py:142). One was committed by accident in e5dff4b8 at
# 31,586 lines; this keeps the next one out.
ignite/team-kit/coord-candidate*.py

# Supervisor registry — RUNTIME state, one live row per supervised sitting, written by the
# spawn/check-in/reap doors as the daemon runs. spec-supervisor pins the file beside its own
# module, so it lands inside the source tree; committing it would ship one box's live process
# table as another box's boot state, and boot re-adopt would then classify strangers' pids.
ignite/supervisor/registry.jsonl
ignite/supervisor/registry.jsonl.tmp-*

# Attempt-counter ledger — RUNTIME state beside the same module, for the same reason: it records
# how many times THIS box's drivers retried. Committing it would hand another box a count it never
# earned, and a counter that arrives already at N disarms a lane nobody ever ran.
ignite/supervisor/attempt-counters.json
ignite/supervisor/attempt-counters.json.tmp

# Provider-lane ledger — RUNTIME state beside the same module, for the same reason as the two
# above: it records THIS box's live provider backoff windows and the reroutes THIS box made.
# Committing it would hand another box a `provider_backoff_until` it never earned, pausing a kill
# clock and suppressing a frozen alarm on a lane that is not backing off at all.
ignite/supervisor/provider-lanes.json
ignite/supervisor/provider-lanes.json.tmp

# Probe-run RUNTIME state, matched at ANY depth. A probe that exercises the watchdog or the
# ending store writes a workspace-shaped `.rbtv/runtime/` beside its own cwd — the worktree root
# for a suite run, the probes folder for a direct run — carrying `heart.db` and
# `outage-ledger.jsonl`. That is THIS box's live run state, never product: committing it would
# hand another box an outage ledger and an ending store it never earned. The repo tracks no
# `.rbtv/` path at all, so the whole tree is ignored rather than its two current leaves.
**/.rbtv/
